  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Veterans Affairs has obligated $3.9B in FY2027 to date on federal contracts. The Department executed 8,291 awards so far, with an average award size of $475K. Obligations are down 95.3% year over year. Annual context shows a multi-year rise through FY26: FY22 obligations were $56.4B, FY23 obligations were $61.7B, FY24 obligations were $66.9B, FY25 obligations were $78.3B, and FY26 obligations were $84.3B. FY27 to date obligations of $3.9B represent partial fiscal-year activity. Top spending categories in FY2027 to date include Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers at $901M, Wired Telecommunications Carriers at $256M, and Other Computer Related Services at $225M. Top vendors for FY2027 to date include TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP at $900M, AT&T ENTERPRISES, LLC at $164M, and ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC at $151M. This snapshot shows where current-year contract dollars are concentrated and how current-year totals compare to full fiscal-year precedent.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has FY2027 spending changed year over year?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $3.9B in FY2027 to date. Obligations are down 95.3% year over year. FY26 obligations were $84.3B, providing direct scale for the change. FY27 totals are partial fiscal-year activity and therefore smaller than prior full-year totals."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where are FY2027 contract dollars concentrated?",
        "body": "Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers is the largest category at $901M, followed by Wired Telecommunications Carriers at $256M and Other Computer Related Services at $225M. TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP is the largest vendor at $900M, with AT&T ENTERPRISES, LLC at $164M and ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC at $151M. The top categories and vendors together account for a large share of the $3.9B obligated so far."
      }
    ]
