  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Veterans Affairs spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Veterans Affairs has obligated $3.9B in contracts in FY2027 to date. The Department executed 8,291 awards so far in FY2027 to date with an average award size of $475K. FY27 totals are partial fiscal-year activity and contrast with full-year obligations of $84.3B in FY26."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Veterans Affairs buy?",
      "a": "The Department of Veterans Affairs buys health and medical insurance services, telecommunications, IT services, construction, and laboratory and medical instruments. Top FY2027 to date categories are Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers at $901M, Wired Telecommunications Carriers at $256M, and Other Computer Related Services at $225M, followed by Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $207M and Computer Systems Design Services at $170M."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Veterans Affairs's largest contractors?",
